Third-party data
----------------

The star catalogue (crates/tuile-star-catalogue/data/bright_stars.parquet,
and the table made from it, crates/tuile-atmosphere/src/stars.table) is
derived from:

  The Bright Star Catalogue, 5th Revised Ed. (Preliminary Version),
  Hoffleit D., Warren Jr W.H., Astronomical Data Center, NSSDC/ADC (1991),
  =1964BS....C......0H, =1991bsc..book.....H.
  Distributed by the CDS, Strasbourg, as catalogue V/50
  (VizieR service, DOI 10.26093/cds/vizier).
  Source: https://cdsarc.cds.unistra.fr/ftp/V/50/catalog.gz
  SHA-256 of catalog.gz: 3dc44b1e90be8fbe5bcc7656032560f51275f985c7e3f783c9028e1838ec7bed
  SHA-256 of catalog:    69797549cc1605aad7ff94e9325e29a1661f2a253917faaa056d9bf20b809afd
  Fetched 2026-10-25.

The CDS states that the copyright of a catalogue depends on its origin and is
given in its ReadMe; the ReadMe of V/50 states no copyright. The catalogue is
a work of NASA's National Space Science Data Center (Astronomical Data
Center). Its authors and the CDS are acknowledged here as the CDS asks.
